Overlay patch 0008: frame/tick cadence probe (wall + eng_ms + gpu_ms + sim_tps
+ thermal), and the real `SohIos_HudStats` for the shell's perf HUD.

Charter 0.3 requires this from day one rather than retrofitted, and requires the
sim-rate metric named honestly. Adapted from the flagship's 0008, with the
BK-specific parts corrected:

* **`sim_tps` is measured against 30, not 60.** Banjo-Kazooie's logic rate is
  `60 / gVIsPerFrame` = **30 Hz** (DECISIONS D6). The probe therefore also
  reports `sim_ratio` = sim_tps / 30, so a healthy run reads 1.00 and the
  "enemies move in slow motion" class of bug is a number, not a feeling.
* **`mode=`** carries BK's current `getGameMode()`. It costs one integer and
  makes every other field interpretable — the attract demo, cutscenes and
  gameplay have genuinely different pacing, and without it a correct 30 fps
  cutscene reading is indistinguishable from a regression. It is also how
  the intro-detection heuristic in 0013 gets verified on a real device.
* **`sub=`** carries the sub-frames-per-tick count. At a 60 fps target the
  engine renders 2 sub-frames per tick, at 120 it renders 4, and cutscenes can
  legitimately cap to 1 (`port_getInterpolationFpsCap`). Without this field a
  correct 30 fps cutscene reads as a regression.

**`tick_fps` vs `render_fps` — the probe measures TICKS, not presents.**
`OnFrame` is called once per `ProcessGfxCommands`, i.e. once per 30 Hz game
tick, and `RunCommands` renders `sub` sub-frames *inside* that call. So
`tick_fps` is the tick rate (identical to `sim_tps` by construction) and the
frame rate a player actually sees is `tick_fps * sub`, reported as
`render_fps`. The original field was named `fps`, which read as the presented
frame rate and understated it by the sub-frame factor — corrected here rather
than left to mislead a future perf claim.

`wall_ms` is the interval between consecutive `ProcessGfxCommands` entries;
`eng_ms` is the time inside `RunCommands`. BOTH include in-call blocking, so
`wall ≈ eng` means blocked-inside (GPU/pacing) while `wall >> eng` means CPU
outside. The name is deliberately not "cpu_ms".

Dependencies, all already in the overlay and asserted present in this fork:
`gSohIosGpuMs` (0028), `gSohIosUpWinBytes`/`Count` (0019/0020),
`SohIos_LibWindowStats`/`PsoWindowStats` (0035), `SohIos_ThermalState` (shell).

Externs are FILE-scope `extern "C"` on purpose — block-scope linkage specs do
not compile in C++, and block-scope externs namespace-mangle. Both cost the
flagship a debugging session.

Match-count asserted against the pristine vendor state.

